********************************************************************************************************************************
* (A) INPUT FILES                                                                                                              *
********************************************************************************************************************************
samples.out                   :: File containing Voronoi models (gets renamed to e.g. samples.out1 for chain 1)
ncells.out                    :: File containing number of cells (gets renamed to e.g. ncells.out1 for chain 1)
sigmas.out                    :: File containing data noise parameters (gets renamed to e.g. noise.out1 for chain 1)
misfit.out                    :: File containing misfits (gets renamed to e.g. misfit.out1 for chain 1)
aratios.out                   :: File containing acceptance ratios (gets renamed to e.g. aratios.out1 for chain 1)
temper.out                    :: File containing temperature jumps (gets renamed to e.g. temper.out)
residuals.out                 :: File containing residuals (gets renamed to e.g. residuals.out1 for chain 1)
********************************************************************************************************************************
* (B) OUTPUT FILES                                                                                                             *
********************************************************************************************************************************
average.out                   :: Average model
stdev.out                     :: Standard deviation map
median.out                    :: Median model
maximum.out                   :: Maximum-a-posteriori model
harmean.out                   :: Harmonic mean model
root_mean_square.out          :: Root-mean-square model
entropy.out                   :: Entropy map
skewness.out                  :: Skewness map
kurtosis.out                  :: Kurtosis map
ncells_iter.out               :: Number of cells as a function of iteration number
misfit_iter.out               :: Misfit as a function of iteration number
posterior_ncells.out          :: Posterior distribution on number of cells
posterior_noise.out           :: Posterior distribution on data noise
posterior_resistivity.out     :: Posterior distribution on resistivities
node_density.out              :: Density of Voronoi nuclei
first.out                     :: First Voronoi model (initial point of Markov chain)
last.out                      :: Last Voronoi model (final point of Markov chain)
residuals_histo.out           :: Residuals
********************************************************************************************************************************
* (C) PROCESSING PARAMETERS                                                                                                    *
********************************************************************************************************************************
0                             :: Output maps in vtx format (=0) or xyz format (=1)
401   1   121                 :: Number of resistivity pixels in x,y,z
5   5   5                     :: Size of x,y,z pixels for calculation of Voronoi centre density
150                           :: Number of pixels in resistivity posterior
100                           :: Number of pixels in noise posterior
401                           :: Number of pixels in residuals
100  200                      :: Only consider residuals whose absolute value is less than this
********************************************************************************************************************************
* (D) MARKOV CHAIN PARAMETERS                                                                                                  *
********************************************************************************************************************************
1500                          :: Burn-in period
10                            :: Thinning of the chain
-1                            :: Stop taking samples at this chain iteration number (-1 to use whole chain)
0                             :: Number of "bad" Markov chains to ignore (=0 if all chains are to be used)
1                             :: Markov chains to ignore (chain numbers one below the other)
2
********************************************************************************************************************************
